== A  conservation: w_off and the slope of a0(z)
PASS A1 w_off = -1 + (2/3) d ln a0/d ln(1+z) from continuity
PASS A2 for a0 ~ (1+z)^q: w_off = -1 + 2q/3 (q = 0 flat -> w = -1; q = 3/2 -> w = 0)
PASS A3 MUTATION: if the offset had w = -1 with a0 rising as (1+z)^(3/2), continuity would be violated (rho_off ~ (1+z)^3 needs w = 0)

== B  a0 = xi H(z) with offset = dark energy is Einstein-de Sitter
PASS B1 with rho_off = Omega_off * 3H^2/(8 pi G) (Omega_off constant, from a0 ~ H) the expansion law is H^2 = H0^2 (1+z)^3 for ANY Omega_off (matter era forever)
PASS B2 deceleration parameter q = +1/2 at all z (no acceleration)
